const e="What to Expect from a Child Psychologist in Brisbane | Michelle Barratt Psychology",t="When something feels different with your child and you can’t quite put your finger on it, it might be time to slow down and take a closer look. A child psycho",s='<!--$--><section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-plum to-rose text-white"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20"><div><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-6"><ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-white/75"><li><a class="hover:text-white" href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3 w-3"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></li><li><a class="hover:text-white active" href="/blog" data-status="active" aria-current="page">Blog</a></li><li aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3 w-3"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></li><li class="text-white" aria-current="page">What to Expect from a Child Psychologist in Brisbane</li></ol></nav><p class="text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-white/85 mb-3">14 November 2025</p><h1 class="text-white text-[32px] md:text-[44px] font-semibold leading-[1.08] max-w-3xl">What to Expect from a Child Psychologist in Brisbane</h1><div class="h-[3px] w-16 bg-sun my-5" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="max-w-2xl text-[16px] md:text-[17px] text-white/95 space-y-3"><p>When something feels different with your child and you can’t quite put your finger on it, it might be time to slow down and take a closer look. A child psychologist helps with that. We work with kids to understand what’s happening behind ch</p></div><div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-white text-plum hover:bg-blush " href="/contact">Contact Us</a></div></div></div></section><section class="bg-soft !py-0"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="py-14 md:py-16"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/getty-images-FT1rzr0K1R4-unsplash.jpg" alt="" class="w-full aspect-[16/9] max-h-[520px] object-cover rounded border border-lilac"/></div></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">When something feels different with your child and you can’t quite put your finger on it, it might be time to slow down and take a closer look. A child psychologist helps with that. We work with kids to understand what’s happening behind changes in mood, behaviour, school stress, or even sleep.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Right before the end of the school year, especially in Brisbane, families often notice these changes more. Routines get messy, term pressure builds up, and tiredness shows up in ways that are hard to manage. If you’ve been thinking about getting support, here’s what to expect when working with a child psychologist in Brisbane.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">When You Might Need Support for Your Child</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Kids don’t always use words to show they’re not okay. Often, it’s how they act that tells us something’s off. You might notice your child:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Getting angry faster than usual or having more outbursts</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Avoiding friends or staying quiet for long stretches</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Struggling to fall asleep or sleeping more than usual</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Dreading school or complaining of stomach aches often</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">As the school year ends and holidays approach, these things can feel sharper. There’s more going on, less structure, and emotions tend to bubble up. For families in Brisbane, this time of year often brings school events, warm-weather gatherings, and changes to routine, and that’s a lot for kids to process. Reaching out for help doesn’t mean your child is broken. It means something’s been hard, and we’re ready to take that seriously.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">What Happens in a Psychology Session for Kids</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">If you’ve never taken your child to a psychologist, it’s normal to feel unsure about what actually happens there. The first session usually begins with chatting with the parent or caregiver. We ask about what’s been going on, when it started, and what you’re hoping to sort through. Depending on age, your child might then join in or have their own time with us separately.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">We focus on making it feel safe and low-pressure. That helps kids open up in their own way. Sometimes we use drawing, games, or play-based tools, whatever gets them talking and feeling understood. Some kids warm up quickly, others take a little longer. That’s okay. We move at their pace.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Whether or not parents stay in the room depends on things like age, situation, and comfort. We’ll talk that through with you, so you’re part of the process and nothing is a surprise.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">How Psychologists Work with Families and Schools</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Helping a child feel better doesn’t stop when they leave the session room. It often helps to bring in other parts of their world, too, like family life or school. When it’s useful, we might connect with teachers or support staff, with your consent. This can help make sure the help your child gets in sessions carries into their day-to-day.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">We might suggest small routines at home or tools your child can use when things feel tricky. Parents can also get tips on how to support change, which can be as simple as how to respond when your child shuts down or how to ease tension at bedtime.</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>We work with parents to keep routines calm and steady</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>We help kids practise tools they can use in real-life moments</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>We link with schools when needed, especially if classroom struggles show up</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">It’s all about giving the child more support behind the scenes so they don’t feel like they’re doing it all alone.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">What Makes a Good Fit: Picking the Right Psychologist for Your Child</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Every child is different, and that means not every match is the right one. A good child psychologist will have experience working with children of different ages and will know how to help them feel safe and seen.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Look for someone who speaks plainly, listens well, and doesn’t rush the process. Trust comes slowly for many kids, and that’s okay. Kids may not open up right away, and that doesn’t mean the support isn’t working; it just means it’s still building.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">For families here in Brisbane, location often matters too. Having someone nearby or who understands local schools and patterns can make things a bit easier. It also means there’s less pressure getting to appointments, which helps when life already feels full.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Michelle Barratt Psychology: Individualised and Evidence-Based Child Support</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">We offer psychological support for children and families from our clinics in Toowong and Wynnum West. Our child psychologists use evidence-based therapies, including cognitive behavioural strategies tailored to each child’s developmental level and unique strengths.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Our practice is led by a Fellow of the Clinical College at the Australian Psychological Society and provides assessment and intervention for a wide range of concerns, including anxiety, school refusal, and behavioural challenges, as well as support for neurodevelopmental conditions.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Common Worries Parents Might Have, and Why They’re Okay</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">It’s normal to feel nervous before that first call or visit. Many parents wonder things like:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>What if I’m judged for how my child is acting?</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>What if I don’t know how to explain the problem?</span></li><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>What if my child refuses to talk?</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">These thoughts come up a lot, and none of them make you a bad parent. Starting support doesn’t mean having all the answers. Our role is to walk beside you as you figure things out. We’re not here to point out what’s wrong but to help find out what’s been hard, and how we can make it lighter.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Sometimes the first step feels like the biggest one. But often, once things get started, that weight begins to shift.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Supporting Your Child’s Wellbeing, One Step at a Time</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">It’s hard seeing your child upset, worried, or stuck in patterns that don’t feel right. But change doesn’t have to come all at once. With the right support, small steps can lead to steady shifts. Many families go through moments like this, even if it seems quiet from the outside. You’re not alone in feeling like something’s off or harder than usual. Acknowledging that is a strong first move. When we listen closely, slow things down, and stay patient with the process, kids tend to find their way through. And we’re here to help them do just that, one small step at a time.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Taking the first step towards supporting your child’s emotional well-being is crucial. If you’re noticing signs that your child might need additional support, consider reaching out to a child psychologist in Brisbane who can help navigate these challenges. At Michelle Barratt Psychology, we prioritise your child’s comfort and tailor our approach to suit their unique needs. Let us partner with you to restore balance and resilience in your family’s daily life. Contact us today to begin the journey.</p></div></section><section class="bg-blush "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold mb-8">More articles</h2><div class="grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"><a class="group bg-white rounded overflow-hidden border border-lilac flex flex-col transition-shadow duration-300 hover:shadow-lg" href="/blog/recognising-ptsd-counselling-needs"><div class="aspect-[3/2] bg-lilac overflow-hidden"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/recognising-ptsd-counselling-needs-featured.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"/></div><div class="p-6 flex flex-col flex-1"><p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-rose mb-2">23 October 2026</p><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold leading-snug">Recognising PTSD Counselling Needs in Toowong Adults</h3><p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 line-clamp-3">Post-traumatic stress disorder, or PTSD, is not only something that happens to people in movies or in extreme situations. It can grow quietly in everyday lif…</p><span class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ocean">Read article<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></span></div></a><a class="group bg-white rounded overflow-hidden border border-lilac flex flex-col transition-shadow duration-300 hover:shadow-lg" href="/blog/online-therapy-in-brisbane-when-you"><div class="aspect-[3/2] bg-lilac overflow-hidden"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/online-therapy-in-brisbane-when-you-featured.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"/></div><div class="p-6 flex flex-col flex-1"><p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-rose mb-2">16 October 2026</p><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold leading-snug">Online Therapy in Brisbane When You Can’t Find Local Support</h3><p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 line-clamp-3">Trying to find a psychologist in Brisbane can feel exhausting. You search, you join waitlists, you juggle your calendar, and still there is no appointment th…</p><span class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ocean">Read article<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></span></div></a><a class="group bg-white rounded overflow-hidden border border-lilac flex flex-col transition-shadow duration-300 hover:shadow-lg" href="/blog/recognising-trauma-counselling-needs"><div class="aspect-[3/2] bg-lilac overflow-hidden"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/recognising-trauma-counselling-needs-featured.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"/></div><div class="p-6 flex flex-col flex-1"><p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-rose mb-2">9 October 2026</p><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold leading-snug">Recognising Trauma Counselling Needs in Toowong Professionals</h3><p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80 line-clamp-3">High-performing professionals in Toowong are often good at holding it together. Work is busy, the pressure is high, and most people tell themselves it is jus…</p><span class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ocean">Read article<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></span></div></a></div></div></section><section class="bg-blush"><div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-14 md:py-16 text-center"><p class="text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-rose mb-2.5">Take the first step</p><h2 class="text-[30px] md:text-[40px] font-semibold leading-[1.1]">Ready to Take the First Step?</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-4 mx-auto" aria-hidden="true"></div><p class="mt-5 text-[17px]">Seeking support can feel overwhelming, but you do not have to navigate life&#x27;s challenges alone. Our administration team can help answer your questions, explain appointment options and connect you with a suitable practitioner.</p><p class="mt-3">Prefer to call? Phone our administration team on <a class="text-ocean underline underline-offset-4 font-medium" href="tel:0731850040">07 3185 0040</a>.</p><div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-rose text-white hover:bg-[#9d2a59] " href="/practitioners">Book Online</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-ocean text-white hover:bg-[#095a6f] " href="/contact">Contact Us</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 border border-plum text-plum hover:bg-lilac " href="/therapy-services">Explore Services</a></div><p class="mt-5 text-sm text-ink/70">If in crisis, please call 000.</p></div></section><!--/$-->',i={title:e,description:t,html:s};export{i as default,t as description,s as html,e as title};
